{
  "id": "implicit-curve-slope",
  "title": "Implicit Curve Slope: dy/dx = −F_x / F_y",
  "eyebrow": "implicit differentiation",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 61,
  "topic": "When a curve is given implicitly by F(x, y) = c, you cannot always solve for y. But the tangent slope at any point is still computable: differentiate the relation, get F_x + F_y · dy/dx = 0, so dy/dx = −F_x / F_y. Slide a point around the level curve and watch the tangent rotate, with the formula's two partials updating live.",
  "subject_id": "mat2b",
  "chapter_number": 5,
  "prerequisites": [
    "gradient-and-level-curves"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "manimoIntro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 6.91,
      "narration": "When y is tangled up with x — no clean formula y of x — can we still get the slope? Yes.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "manimo-enter",
            "content": "Manimo enters centre",
            "delay": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Tangled? Differentiate anyway.",
            "delay": 0.7,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "right of Manimo, serif italic"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "setup",
      "start": 6.91,
      "end": 20.24,
      "narration": "Take an example. F of x and y equals x squared plus x y plus y squared. Set it equal to three. The solution set is a closed curve — a tilted ellipse.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "left-right",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "graph-axes",
            "content": "xy axes centred",
            "delay": 0.3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)"
          },
          {
            "type": "graph-curve",
            "content": "Tilted ellipse F(x,y) = 3",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "F(x, y) = x² + x y + y²",
            "delay": 1.8,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "right panel"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "F(x, y) = 3",
            "delay": 2.8,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "right panel below F"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "no clean y = …(x)",
            "delay": 4,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)",
            "position": "right panel"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "derive",
      "start": 20.24,
      "end": 36.14,
      "narration": "Differentiate both sides with respect to x, treating y as a function of x. The partial in x plus the partial in y times dy by dx equals zero. Solve: dy by dx equals minus the partial in x over the partial in y.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "left-right",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "graph-marker",
            "content": "Point P on the curve at one example position",
            "delay": 0.3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Tangent line at P, slope = -F_x / F_y",
            "delay": 3.2,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "F_x + F_y · dy/dx = 0",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)",
            "position": "right panel — derivation step 1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "dy/dx = −F_x / F_y",
            "delay": 3.8,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "right panel — payoff"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "F_x = 2x + y",
            "delay": 5,
            "color": "var(--violet-400)",
            "position": "right panel — derivative table"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "F_y = x + 2y",
            "delay": 5.6,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)",
            "position": "right panel — derivative table"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sweep",
      "start": 36.14,
      "end": 52.01,
      "narration": "Now slide the point all the way around the curve. The tangent rotates with it. Where the partial in y vanishes the tangent is vertical — undefined slope. Where the partial in x vanishes the tangent is flat. The formula handles every position.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "left-right",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "graph-marker",
            "content": "P moves around the ellipse",
            "delay": 0,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Tangent line rotating with P",
            "delay": 0,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "live readout: F_x, F_y, dy/dx",
            "delay": 0.4,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "right panel — values update each frame"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Annotate vertical tangent at F_y = 0",
            "delay": 4,
            "color": "var(--rose-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Annotate horizontal tangent at F_x = 0",
            "delay": 8,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "takeaway",
      "start": 52.01,
      "end": 61,
      "narration": "The level curve hides the function y of x. Implicit differentiation reads the slope without ever isolating it.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-title",
            "content": "Slope without solving.",
            "delay": 0.2,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "centre serif italic large"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "dy/dx = −F_x / F_y",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "centre large"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Two partial derivatives, one ratio, every tangent.",
            "delay": 2.4,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)",
            "position": "centre below"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
